A||||3||fiero56||tire diameter for speedo calibration(stock)||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||05-26-2001||04:04 PM||||This is probably a little too techincal/nit-picky, but I am trying to determine what tire diameter Pontiac was using for calibrating the speedo. I've got un-sprung(and sprung) tire diamter numbers here in front of me that I have calculated, but I'm wondering what numbers the Pontiac engineers were using. I assume they used the same number for all 5 years of production, I just need to know what diamter they used.||||reg||5
Z||000001||cadaver||05-26-2001||05:54 PM||||Why. Cant you just figure out how much it off and change the speedo gears accordingly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||05-26-2001||06:05 PM||||Weeeeellll, I have stock wheels and stock tire sizes on my stock Fieros. My stock speedo is still set at stock factory settings, but need to know what stock tire diameter Pontiac was using.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-26-2001||09:51 PM||||There are 3 different gear colors. The 13" wheels had 1 color, the 14" 60's had another color and the 14" 70's and 15" 60's had another. The gear is on the VSS in the trans. Interchanging them onlt affects the speedo by about 1%.<P>Follow the link to a Tire Calculator.<BR>It will tell you what size tires you can use and how it affects the speedo.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> <P>Just type in the stock rear tire size and the tire you want to go to and it'll show you the difference in size (diameter and width) and show you speedo correction %.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">     <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||1
